            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ritaadu"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used course kosher salt instead of regular salt. I suggest putting the ingredients in a ziploc bag to allow for even distribution on the potatoes. The coating is so good until you can enjoy just a few and eat off of these for an entire week.",
            "datePublished": "2014-02-14T11:41:54.530Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brandie McCollum"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used 12 large fingerling potatoes, halved, 1.5 large carrots and a small piece of Daikon instead of just potatoes. I didn't have fresh basil. Added Fried Garlic in addition to the fresh garlic which gave it a added depth of flavor. Halved the amount of salt, I used Himalayan Pink Sea Salt fresh ground, perfect amount, any more would be too salty. I would halve the amount of red pepper flakes next time too as I felt they overwhelmed the other herbs a little bit, but still AMAZING first run. The best oven roasted potatoes Ive tasted!!!",
            "datePublished": "2018-01-01T19:20:17.827Z"
          },
          {
